IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg7-governing-provisions`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1, ss 255 to 258 -- MERGER OR CONSOLIDATION OF NONSTOCK CORPORATIONS: nonstock with
-- nonstock (s 255), domestic with foreign nonstock (s 256), stock with nonstock (s 257), domestic with foreign stock and nonstock (s 258).
-- Source: de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt (a converter's plain-text rendering, not the official text); `-- src:N | ...` quotes line N.
--
-- The four sections are one shape: who may merge or consolidate (subsection (a)); what the agreement states and how it is executed
-- (subsection (b)); how it is approved, noticed, certified, filed and made effective (subsection (c), or for a corporation with no
-- voting members but the governing body, (d)); which provisions of ss 251 and 252 apply by reference; and the limit on a charitable
-- nonstock corporation losing its charitable status. Sections 256 to 258 send the approval of a Delaware corporation back to s 255
-- (nonstock) or s 251 (stock, piece dg6): that outcome is a plain input there.
--
-- Reading of the nonstock words (s 114(a), piece dg1; KEEL fork F13): "stockholders" are "members", "board of directors" is "governing body",
-- "stock" is "memberships or membership interests". The core's `the outstanding stock entitled to vote` stands for the members entitled to
-- vote, and `the whole board` for the governing body.
-- OUT OF RANGE (plain inputs): s 103 (execution, acknowledgment, filing, effective time: dg1), s 155 (fractions of shares: dg3), s 251(c) to (f)
-- (dg6), s 252(c), (d) (dg6), s 391(a)(29) (the fee: dg11), the laws of other jurisdictions.
-- "Facts" sentences (src:1181, 1199, 1216): encoded as `s 255(b) the thing is a fact in the sense of the sentence that defines facts`, fork F-facts-1;
-- the rule they sit beside (a term may depend on facts outside the agreement if the manner is clearly and expressly set forth) is encoded too.

§ `dg7 The nouns of ss 255 to 258`

-- A constituent corporation, as these sections tell them apart: its kind (stock, nonstock, nonprofit, charitable) and where it is formed.
-- src:1173 | Any 2 or more nonstock corporations of this State, whether or not organized for profit, may merge into a single surviving corporation, which may be any 1 of the constituent corporations, or they may consolidate into a new resulting nonstock corporation, whether or not organized for profit, formed by the consolidation, pursuant to an agreement of merger or consolidation, as the case may be, complying and approved in accordance with this section …
-- src:1190 | Any 1 or more nonstock corporations of this State may merge or consolidate with 1 or more foreign nonstock corporations, unless the laws of the jurisdiction or jurisdictions under which such foreign nonstock corporation or corporations are organized prohibit such merger or consolidation. The constituent corporations may merge into a single surviving corporation, which may be any 1 of the constituent corporations, or they may consolidate into a new resulting nonstock corporation formed by the consolidation, which may be a corporation of the jurisdiction of organization of any 1 of the constituent corporations, pursuant to an agreement of merger or consolidation, as the case may be, complying and approved in accordance with this section. The term “foreign nonstock corporation” means a nonstock corporation organized under the laws of any jurisdiction other than this State …
-- src:1208 | Any 1 or more nonstock corporations of this State, whether or not organized for profit …
-- src:1224 | Any 1 or more corporations of this State, whether stock or nonstock corporations and whether or not organized for profit, may merge or consolidate with 1 or more foreign corporations …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 255(a) (src:1173); § 256(a) (src:1190); § 257(a) (src:1208); § 258(a) (src:1224)
DECLARE `dg7 Constituent corporation` HAS
    `kind of corporation`            IS A `Kind of corporation`
    `where the corporation is formed` IS A `Where an entity is formed`

-- A merger (into a surviving corporation that is one of the constituent corporations) or a consolidation (into a new resulting corporation).
-- src:1173 | may merge into a single surviving corporation, which may be any 1 of the constituent corporations, or they may consolidate into a new resulting nonstock corporation, whether or not organized for profit, formed by the consolidation …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 255(a) (src:1173)
DECLARE `dg7 Merger or consolidation` IS ONE OF
    `a merger into a surviving corporation that is one of the constituent corporations`
    `a consolidation into a new resulting corporation formed by the consolidation`

-- What the agreement states. One record serves ss 255(b), 256(b), 257(b) and 258(b): each section's rule reads the fields it names.
-- src:1175 | (1) The terms and conditions of the merger or consolidation;
-- src:1176 | (2) The mode of carrying the same into effect;
-- src:1177 | (3) In the case of a merger, such amendments or changes in the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation as are desired to be effected by the merger (which amendments or changes may amend and restate the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation in its entirety), or, if no such amendments or changes are desired, a statement that the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation shall be its certificate of incorporation;
-- src:1178 | (4) In the case of a consolidation, that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation shall be as is set forth in an attachment to the agreement;
-- src:1179 | (5) The manner, if any, of converting the memberships or membership interests of each of the constituent corporations into memberships or membership interests of the corporation surviving or resulting from the merger or consolidation, or of cancelling some or all of such memberships or membership interests, and, if any memberships or membership interests of any of the constituent corporations are not to remain outstanding, to be converted solely into memberships or membership interests of the surviving or resulting corporation or to be cancelled, the cash, property, rights or securities of any other corporation or entity which the holders of such memberships or membership interests are to receive in exchange for, or upon conversion of, such memberships or membership interests …
-- src:1180 | (6) Such other details or provisions as are deemed desirable, including, without limiting the generality of the foregoing, a provision for the payment of cash in lieu of the issuance or recognition of fractional shares, rights or other securities of any other corporation or entity the shares, rights or other securities of which are to be received in the merger or consolidation, or for some other arrangement with respect thereto, consistent with § 155 of this title …
-- src:1198 | (7) Such other provisions or facts as shall be required to be set forth in an agreement of merger or consolidation (including any provision for amendment of the certificate of incorporation (or equivalent document) of a surviving foreign nonstock corporation) by the laws of each jurisdiction under which any of the foreign nonstock corporations are organized …
-- src:1214 | (5) The manner, if any, of converting the shares of stock of a stock corporation and the memberships or membership interests of a nonstock corporation into shares or other securities of a stock corporation or memberships or membership interests of a nonstock corporation surviving or resulting from such merger or consolidation or of cancelling some or all of such shares or memberships or membership interests, and, if any shares of any such stock corporation or memberships or membership interests of any such nonstock corporation are not to remain outstanding, to be converted solely into shares or other securities of the stock corporation or memberships or membership interests of the nonstock corporation surviving or resulting from such merger or consolidation or to be cancelled, the cash, property, rights or securities of any other corporation or entity which the holders of shares of any such stock corporation or memberships or membership interests of any such nonstock corporation are to receive in exchange for, or upon conversion of such shares or memberships or membership interests, and the surrender of any certificates evidencing them …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 255(b) (src:1175-1180); § 256(b) (src:1198); § 257(b) (src:1214)
DECLARE `dg7 Agreement of merger or consolidation` HAS
    `states the terms and conditions of the merger or consolidation`                                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `states the mode of carrying the merger or consolidation into effect`                                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `states the amendments or changes in the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation, or that it shall be its certificate of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `states that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation shall be as set forth in an attachment to the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `some shares, memberships or membership interests are to be converted or cancelled`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `states the manner of converting or cancelling them`                                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `some shares, memberships or membership interests are not to remain outstanding`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `states the cash, property, rights or securities the holders are to receive in exchange for them`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `states the surrender of any certificates evidencing the shares, memberships or membership interests`                    IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 257(b)(5) only
    `provides for the payment of cash in lieu of fractional shares, rights or other securities, or some other arrangement`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `that provision is consistent with s 155`                                                                               IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 155 (piece dg3)
    `states the provisions or facts the laws of each foreign jurisdiction require in an agreement of merger or consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 256(b)(7), s 258(b)

-- The statements common to ss 255(b), 256(b) and 257(b): items (1) to (6).
-- READING F-5: item (5) asks for "the manner, if any, of converting ... or of cancelling" (a statement of the manner, where there is any) and, "if any
-- memberships ... are not to remain outstanding, to be converted solely into memberships ... or to be cancelled, the cash, property, rights or
-- securities ... which the holders ... are to receive in exchange for, or upon conversion of," them. Read: where some do not remain outstanding, the
-- agreement states what the holders get for them. Item (6) is permissive ("as are deemed desirable") and asks only that a cash-in-lieu provision be
-- consistent with s 155.
-- src:1175 | (1) The terms and conditions of the merger or consolidation;
-- src:1176 | (2) The mode of carrying the same into effect;
-- src:1177 | (3) In the case of a merger, such amendments or changes in the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation as are desired to be effected by the merger (which amendments or changes may amend and restate the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation in its entirety), or, if no such amendments or changes are desired, a statement that the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation shall be its certificate of incorporation …
-- src:1178 | (4) In the case of a consolidation, that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation shall be as is set forth in an attachment to the agreement …
-- src:1179 | (5) The manner, if any, of converting the memberships or membership interests of each of the constituent corporations into memberships or membership interests of the corporation surviving or resulting from the merger or consolidation, or of cancelling some or all of such memberships or membership interests, and, if any memberships or membership interests of any of the constituent corporations are not to remain outstanding, to be converted solely into memberships or membership interests of the surviving or resulting corporation or to be cancelled, the cash, property, rights or securities of any other corporation or entity which the holders of such memberships or membership interests are to receive in exchange for, or upon conversion of, such memberships or membership interests …
-- src:1180 | (6) Such other details or provisions as are deemed desirable, including, without limiting the generality of the foregoing, a provision for the payment of cash in lieu of the issuance or recognition of fractional shares, rights or other securities of any other corporation or entity the shares, rights or other securities of which are to be received in the merger or consolidation, or for some other arrangement with respect thereto, consistent with § 155 of this title …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 255(b)(1) to (6) (src:1175-1180)
GIVEN kind IS A `dg7 Merger or consolidation`
      ag IS A `dg7 Agreement of merger or consolidation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`dg7 s 255(b)(1) to (6) the agreement states what items (1) to (6) require` kind ag MEANS
        ag's `states the terms and conditions of the merger or consolidation`
    AND ag's `states the mode of carrying the merger or consolidation into effect`
    AND (IF kind EQUALS `a merger into a surviving corporation that is one of the constituent corporations`
         THEN ag's `states the amendments or changes in the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation, or that it shall be its certificate of incorporation`
         ELSE ag's `states that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation shall be as set forth in an attachment to the agreement`)
    AND (   (NOT ag's `some shares, memberships or membership interests are to be converted or cancelled`)
         OR ag's `states the manner of converting or cancelling them`)
    AND (   (NOT ag's `some shares, memberships or membership interests are not to remain outstanding`)
         OR ag's `states the cash, property, rights or securities the holders are to receive in exchange for them`)
    AND (   (NOT ag's `provides for the payment of cash in lieu of fractional shares, rights or other securities, or some other arrangement`)
         OR ag's `that provision is consistent with s 155`)

§ `s 255 Merger or consolidation of domestic nonstock corporations`

-- (a) "Any 2 or more nonstock corporations of this State, whether or not organized for profit, may merge into a single surviving
-- corporation, which may be any 1 of the constituent corporations, or they may consolidate into a new resulting nonstock corporation,
-- whether or not organized for profit, formed by the consolidation, pursuant to an agreement of merger or consolidation, as the case may
-- be, complying and approved in accordance with this section."
-- src:1190 | The term “foreign nonstock corporation” means a nonstock corporation organized under the laws of any jurisdiction other than this State …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 256(a) (src:1190)
GIVEN c IS A `dg7 Constituent corporation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 256(a) a foreign nonstock corporation` c MEANS
        `the kind is a nonstock corporation` (c's `kind of corporation`)
    AND (NOT c's `where the corporation is formed` EQUALS `this State`)

-- src:1173 | Any 2 or more nonstock corporations of this State, whether or not organized for profit, may merge into a single surviving corporation, which may be any 1 of the constituent corporations, or they may consolidate into a new resulting nonstock corporation, whether or not organized for profit, formed by the consolidation, pursuant to an agreement of merger or consolidation, as the case may be, complying and approved in accordance with this section …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 255(a) (src:1173)
GIVEN c IS A `dg7 Constituent corporation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 255(a) the corporation is a nonstock corporation of this State` c MEANS
        `the kind is a nonstock corporation` (c's `kind of corporation`)
    AND c's `where the corporation is formed` EQUALS `this State`

-- src:1173 | Any 2 or more nonstock corporations of this State, whether or not organized for profit, may merge into a single surviving corporation, which may be any 1 of the constituent corporations, or they may consolidate into a new resulting nonstock corporation, whether or not organized for profit, formed by the consolidation, pursuant to an agreement of merger or consolidation, as the case may be, complying and approved in accordance with this section …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 255(a) (src:1173)
GIVEN constituents IS A LIST OF `dg7 Constituent corporation`
      kind IS A `dg7 Merger or consolidation`
      `the surviving corporation is one of the constituent corporations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resulting corporation is a new nonstock corporation formed by the consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement complies, and is approved, in accordance with this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 255(a) the corporations may merge or consolidate` constituents kind `the surviving corporation is one of the constituent corporations` `the resulting corporation is a new nonstock corporation formed by the consolidation` `the agreement complies, and is approved, in accordance with this section` MEANS
        count constituents AT LEAST 2
    AND all `s 255(a) the corporation is a nonstock corporation of this State` constituents
    AND (IF kind EQUALS `a merger into a surviving corporation that is one of the constituent corporations`
         THEN `the surviving corporation is one of the constituent corporations`
         ELSE `the resulting corporation is a new nonstock corporation formed by the consolidation`)
    AND `the agreement complies, and is approved, in accordance with this section`

-- (b) "Subject to subsection (d) of this section, the governing body of each corporation which desires to merge or consolidate shall
-- adopt a resolution approving an agreement of merger or consolidation. The agreement shall state: (1) to (6)".
-- src:1174 | (b) Subject to subsection (d) of this section, the governing body of each corporation which desires to merge or consolidate shall adopt a resolution approving an agreement of merger or consolidation. The agreement shall state:
@ref 8 Del. C. § 255(b) (src:1174)
GIVEN kind IS A `dg7 Merger or consolidation`
      ag IS A `dg7 Agreement of merger or consolidation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 255(b) the agreement states what the subsection requires` kind ag MEANS
    `dg7 s 255(b)(1) to (6) the agreement states what items (1) to (6) require` kind ag

-- "The agreement so adopted shall be executed by an authorized person, provided that if the agreement is filed, it shall be executed and
-- acknowledged in accordance with s 103 of this title." (out of range: section 103, piece dg1)
-- src:1181 | The agreement so adopted shall be executed by an authorized person, provided that if the agreement is filed, it shall be executed and acknowledged in accordance with § 103 of this title …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 255(b) (src:1181)
GIVEN `the agreement was executed by an authorized person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement is filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement was executed and acknowledged in accordance with s 103` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 255(b) the agreement has been executed as the subsection requires` `the agreement was executed by an authorized person` `the agreement is filed` `the agreement was executed and acknowledged in accordance with s 103` MEANS
        `the agreement was executed by an authorized person`
    AND (   (NOT `the agreement is filed`)
         OR `the agreement was executed and acknowledged in accordance with s 103`)

-- "Any of the terms of the agreement of merger or consolidation may be made dependent upon facts ascertainable outside of such
-- agreement, provided that the manner in which such facts shall operate upon the terms of the agreement is clearly and expressly set
-- forth in the agreement". The same proviso is in ss 256(b), 257(b) and, for the provisions of s 261(a), in s 261(a).
-- src:1181 | Any of the terms of the agreement of merger or consolidation may be made dependent upon facts ascertainable outside of such agreement, provided that the manner in which such facts shall operate upon the terms of the agreement is clearly and expressly set forth in the agreement of merger or consolidation …
-- src:1199 | Any of the terms of the agreement of merger or consolidation may be made dependent upon facts ascertainable outside of such agreement, provided that the manner in which such facts shall operate upon the terms of the agreement is clearly and expressly set forth in the agreement of merger or consolidation …
-- src:1216 | Any of the terms of the agreement of merger or consolidation may be made dependent upon facts ascertainable outside of such agreement, provided that the manner in which such facts shall operate upon the terms of the agreement is clearly and expressly set forth in the agreement of merger or consolidation …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 255(b) (src:1181); § 256(b) (src:1199); § 257(b) (src:1216)
GIVEN `the manner in which the facts operate upon the terms is clearly and expressly set forth in the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 255(b) a term of the agreement may be made dependent upon facts ascertainable outside the agreement` `the manner in which the facts operate upon the terms is clearly and expressly set forth in the agreement` MEANS
    `the manner in which the facts operate upon the terms is clearly and expressly set forth in the agreement`

-- The sentence that follows the proviso in each of ss 255(b), 256(b) and 257(b): "The term 'facts,' as used in the preceding sentence, includes,
-- but is not limited to, the occurrence of any event, including a determination or action by any person or body, including the corporation."
-- Fork F-facts-1: "includes, but is not limited to" makes the list open. An event, a determination by a person or body, and an action by a
-- person or body (the corporation included) are facts; for anything else the sentence neither says that it is nor that it is not: NOTHING.
-- src:1181 | The term “facts,” as used in the preceding sentence, includes, but is not limited to, the occurrence of any event, including a determination or action by any person or body, including the corporation.
-- src:1199 | The term “facts,” as used in the preceding sentence, includes, but is not limited to, the occurrence of any event, including a determination or action by any person or body, including the corporation.
-- src:1216 | The term “facts,” as used in the preceding sentence, includes, but is not limited to, the occurrence of any event, including a determination or action by any person or body, including the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 255(b) (src:1181); § 256(b) (src:1199); § 257(b) (src:1216)
DECLARE `dg7 Thing a term of the agreement may be made dependent upon` IS ONE OF
    `the occurrence of an event`
    `a determination by a person or body, including the corporation`
    `an action by a person or body, including the corporation`
    `something that is neither an event, a determination nor an action`

GIVEN thing IS A `dg7 Thing a term of the agreement may be made dependent upon`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 255(b) the thing is a fact in the sense of the sentence that defines facts` thing MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `the occurrence of an event` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a determination by a person or body, including the corporation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an action by a person or body, including the corporation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `something that is neither an event, a determination nor an action` THEN NOTHING

-- (c) Notice. "Due notice of the time, place and purpose of the meeting shall be given to each member of each such corporation who has
-- the right to vote for the election of the members of the governing body of the corporation and to each other member who is entitled
-- to vote on the merger under the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws of such corporation, at the member's address as it appears
-- on the records of the corporation, at least 20 days prior to the date of the meeting. The notice shall contain a copy of the agreement
-- or a brief summary thereof."
-- src:1182 | Due notice of the time, place and purpose of the meeting shall be given to each member of each such corporation who has the right to vote for the election of the members of the governing body of the corporation and to each other member who is entitled to vote on the merger under the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws of such corporation …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 255(c) (src:1182)
GIVEN `the member has the right to vote for the election of the members of the governing body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member is entitled to vote on the merger under the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 255(c) the member is owed notice of the meeting` `the member has the right to vote for the election of the members of the governing body` `the member is entitled to vote on the merger under the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws` MEANS
        `the member has the right to vote for the election of the members of the governing body`
    OR `the member is entitled to vote on the merger under the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws`

-- src:1182 | at least 20 days prior to the date of the meeting …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 255(c) (src:1182)
GIVEN `the date of the meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 255(c) the latest date for the notice of the meeting` `the date of the meeting` MEANS
    `the date` (`period in days` 20) `before` `the date of the meeting`

-- src:1182 | Due notice of the time, place and purpose of the meeting shall be given to each member of each such corporation who has the right to vote for the election of the members of the governing body of the corporation and to each other member who is entitled to vote on the merger under the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws of such corporation, at the member’s address as it appears on the records of the corporation, at least 20 days prior to the date of the meeting. The notice shall contain a copy of the agreement or a brief summary thereof …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 255(c) (src:1182)
DECLARE `s 255(c) Notice of the meeting` HAS
    `the date the notice was given`                                                             IS A DATE
    `the date of the meeting`                                                                   IS A DATE
    `the notice states the time of the meeting`                                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice states the place of the meeting`                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice states the purpose of the meeting`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice contains a copy of the agreement`                                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice contains a brief summary of the agreement`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice was sent to the member's address as it appears on the records of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1182 | Due notice of the time, place and purpose of the meeting shall be given to each member of each such corporation who has the right to vote for the election of the members of the governing body of the corporation and to each other member who is entitled to vote on the merger under the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws of such corporation, at the member’s address as it appears on the records of the corporation, at least 20 days prior to the date of the meeting. The notice shall contain a copy of the agreement or a brief summary thereof …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 255(c) (src:1182)
GIVEN n IS A `s 255(c) Notice of the meeting`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 255(c) the notice satisfies the subsection` n MEANS
        n's `the date the notice was given` AT MOST `s 255(c) the latest date for the notice of the meeting` (n's `the date of the meeting`)
    AND n's `the notice states the time of the meeting`
    AND n's `the notice states the place of the meeting`
    AND n's `the notice states the purpose of the meeting`
    AND (   n's `the notice contains a copy of the agreement`
         OR n's `the notice contains a brief summary of the agreement`)
    AND n's `the notice was sent to the member's address as it appears on the records of the corporation`

-- The vote. "If the agreement is adopted by a majority of the members of each such corporation entitled to vote for the election of the
-- members of the governing body of the corporation and any other members entitled to vote on the merger under the certificate of
-- incorporation or the bylaws of such corporation". READING F-255-1: one body of voters (the members entitled to vote for the governing body
-- together with any others entitled to vote on the merger), and a majority of ALL of them, not of those present. (The other reading, a
-- separate majority of each group, is recorded in the fork register.) A majority is more than half (KEEL fork F4); counts that cannot
-- be a vote answer NOTHING.
-- src:1182 | If the agreement is adopted by a majority of the members of each such corporation entitled to vote for the election of the members of the governing body of the corporation and any other members entitled to vote on the merger under the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws of such corporation, then …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 255(c) (src:1182)
GIVEN `the number of members entitled to vote on the agreement` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those members who voted for adoption` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 255(c) the members of the corporation have adopted the agreement` `the number of members entitled to vote on the agreement` `the number of those members who voted for adoption` MEANS
    `the vote carries` (`a majority of` `the outstanding stock entitled to vote`) `the number of those members who voted for adoption` `the number of members entitled to vote on the agreement`

-- "then that fact shall be certified on the agreement by the officer of each such corporation performing the duties ordinarily performed
-- by the secretary or assistant secretary of a corporation, provided that such certification on the agreement shall not be required if a
-- certificate of merger or consolidation is filed in lieu of filing the agreement." The same proviso is in subsection (d).
-- src:1182 | then that fact shall be certified on the agreement by the officer of each such corporation performing the duties ordinarily performed by the secretary or assistant secretary of a corporation, provided that such certification on the agreement shall not be required if a certificate of merger or consolidation is filed in lieu of filing the agreement …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 255(c) (src:1182); § 255(d) (src:1183)
GIVEN `the adoption was certified on the agreement by the officer who performs the duties of the secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a certificate of merger or consolidation is filed in lieu of filing the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 255(c) the adoption has been certified as the subsection requires` `the adoption was certified on the agreement by the officer who performs the duties of the secretary` `a certificate of merger or consolidation is filed in lieu of filing the agreement` MEANS
        `the adoption was certified on the agreement by the officer who performs the duties of the secretary`
    OR `a certificate of merger or consolidation is filed in lieu of filing the agreement`

-- (d) "Notwithstanding subsection (b) or (c) of this section, if, under the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws of any 1 or more of
-- the constituent corporations, there shall be no members who have the right to vote for the election of the members of the governing
-- body of the corporation, or for the merger, other than the members of the governing body themselves, no further action by the
-- governing body or the members of such corporation shall be necessary if the resolution approving an agreement of merger or
-- consolidation has been adopted by a majority of all the members of the governing body thereof". The base is the whole governing body.
-- src:1183 | (d) Notwithstanding subsection (b) or (c) of this section, if, under the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws of any 1 or more of the constituent corporations, there shall be no members who have the right to vote for the election of the members of the governing body of the corporation, or for the merger, other than the members of the governing body themselves, no further action by the governing body or the members of such corporation shall be necessary if the resolution approving an agreement of merger or consolidation has been adopted by a majority of all the members of the governing body thereof …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 255(d) (src:1183)
GIVEN `no member other than the members of the governing body themselves has the right to vote for the election of the members of the governing body or for the merger` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of members of the governing body` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of members of the governing body who adopted the resolution` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 255(d) the governing body alone has approved the agreement` `no member other than the members of the governing body themselves has the right to vote for the election of the members of the governing body or for the merger` `the number of members of the governing body` `the number of members of the governing body who adopted the resolution` MEANS
    IF NOT `no member other than the members of the governing body themselves has the right to vote for the election of the members of the governing body or for the merger`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE `the vote carries` (`a majority of` `the whole board`) `the number of members of the governing body who adopted the resolution` `the number of members of the governing body`

-- What one constituent corporation must have done: the resolution of the governing body and the members' adoption (subsections (b) and
-- (c)), or in the case of subsection (d) the governing body's majority alone; and the certification.
-- src:1174 | (b) Subject to subsection (d) of this section, the governing body of each corporation which desires to merge or consolidate shall adopt a resolution approving an agreement of merger or consolidation …
-- src:1182 | (c) Subject to subsection (d) of this section, the agreement shall be submitted to the members of each constituent corporation, at an annual or special meeting thereof for the purpose of acting on the agreement …
-- src:1183 | (d) Notwithstanding subsection (b) or (c) of this section, if, under the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws of any 1 or more of the constituent corporations, there shall be no members who have the right to vote for the election of the members of the governing body of the corporation, or for the merger, other than the members of the governing body themselves, no further action by the governing body or the members of such corporation shall be necessary if the resolution approving an agreement of merger or consolidation has been adopted by a majority of all the members of the governing body thereof …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 255(b) (src:1174); § 255(c) (src:1182); § 255(d) (src:1183)
DECLARE `dg7 s 255 Approval by one constituent corporation` HAS
    `the governing body adopted a resolution approving the agreement`                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `no member other than the members of the governing body themselves has the right to vote for the election of the members of the governing body or for the merger` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of members of the governing body`                                                                          IS A NUMBER
    `the number of members of the governing body who adopted the resolution`                                               IS A NUMBER
    `the number of members entitled to vote on the agreement`                                                              IS A NUMBER
    `the number of those members who voted for adoption`                                                                   IS A NUMBER
    `the adoption was certified on the agreement by the officer who performs the duties of the secretary`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `a certificate of merger or consolidation is filed in lieu of filing the agreement`                                    IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1174 | (b) Subject to subsection (d) of this section, the governing body of each corporation which desires to merge or consolidate shall adopt a resolution approving an agreement of merger or consolidation …
-- src:1182 | (c) Subject to subsection (d) of this section, the agreement shall be submitted to the members of each constituent corporation, at an annual or special meeting thereof for the purpose of acting on the agreement …
-- src:1183 | (d) Notwithstanding subsection (b) or (c) of this section, if, under the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws of any 1 or more of the constituent corporations, there shall be no members who have the right to vote for the election of the members of the governing body of the corporation, or for the merger, other than the members of the governing body themselves, no further action by the governing body or the members of such corporation shall be necessary if the resolution approving an agreement of merger or consolidation has been adopted by a majority of all the members of the governing body thereof …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 255(b) (src:1174); § 255(c) (src:1182); § 255(d) (src:1183)
GIVEN a IS A `dg7 s 255 Approval by one constituent corporation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 255 the constituent corporation has approved the agreement` a MEANS
    IF a's `no member other than the members of the governing body themselves has the right to vote for the election of the members of the governing body or for the merger`
    THEN CONSIDER `s 255(d) the governing body alone has approved the agreement` TRUE (a's `the number of members of the governing body`) (a's `the number of members of the governing body who adopted the resolution`)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST byGoverningBody THEN JUST (       byGoverningBody
                                                 AND `s 255(c) the adoption has been certified as the subsection requires` (a's `the adoption was certified on the agreement by the officer who performs the duties of the secretary`) (a's `a certificate of merger or consolidation is filed in lieu of filing the agreement`))
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 255(c) the members of the corporation have adopted the agreement` (a's `the number of members entitled to vote on the agreement`) (a's `the number of those members who voted for adoption`)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST byMembers THEN JUST (       a's `the governing body adopted a resolution approving the agreement`
                                          AND byMembers
                                          AND `s 255(c) the adoption has been certified as the subsection requires` (a's `the adoption was certified on the agreement by the officer who performs the duties of the secretary`) (a's `a certificate of merger or consolidation is filed in lieu of filing the agreement`))

-- "If the agreement shall be adopted and certified by each constituent corporation in accordance with this section, it shall be filed and
-- shall become effective in accordance with s 103 of this title." The time of effect is s 103's (out of range, piece dg1): taken as the
-- date the filing becomes effective. NOTHING (not effective) if some constituent corporation has not adopted and certified.
-- src:1182 | If the agreement shall be adopted and certified by each constituent corporation in accordance with this section, it shall be filed and shall become effective in accordance with § 103 of this title …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 255(c) (src:1182)
GIVEN approvals IS A LIST OF BOOLEAN
      `the date the filing becomes effective in accordance with s 103` IS A DATE   -- out of range: section 103, piece dg1
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 255(c) the date on which the merger or consolidation becomes effective` approvals `the date the filing becomes effective in accordance with s 103` MEANS
    IF (NOT (null approvals)) AND (and approvals)
    THEN JUST `the date the filing becomes effective in accordance with s 103`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- "The provisions set forth in the last sentence of s 251(c) of this title shall apply to a merger under this section, and the reference
-- therein to stockholder shall be deemed to include member hereunder." The last sentence of s 251(c) lets the surviving or resulting
-- corporation file a certificate of merger or consolidation in lieu of the agreement; that certificate states, among other things, that
-- a copy of the agreement will be furnished, on request and without cost, to any stockholder of any constituent corporation (s 251(c)(7), piece dg6).
-- src:1182 | The provisions set forth in the last sentence of § 251(c) of this title shall apply to a merger under this section, and the reference therein to “stockholder” shall be deemed to include “member” hereunder …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 255(c) (src:1182)
GIVEN `the person is a stockholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 255(c) the person is a stockholder for the purposes of the last sentence of s 251(c)` `the person is a stockholder` `the person is a member` MEANS
        `the person is a stockholder`
    OR `the person is a member`

§ `dg7 Provisions of ss 251 and 252 that ss 255 to 258 bring in`

-- The sections 255 to 258 bring in provisions of s 251 or s 252 (pieces dg6): "shall apply", "insofar as they may be applicable", or "if the
-- corporation surviving the merger is a corporation of this State". This noun names the provision; each section's rule below says
-- whether the provision applies to its mergers. What the provision then decides is the outcome of dg6's rule, taken as an input where a
-- question depends on it.
-- src:1182 | The provisions set forth in the last sentence of § 251(c) of this title shall apply to a merger under this section, and the reference therein to “stockholder” shall be deemed to include “member” hereunder …
-- src:1184 | (e) Section 251(d) of this title shall apply to a merger under this section; provided, however, that references to the board of directors, to stockholders, and to shares of a constituent corporation shall be deemed to be references to the governing body of the corporation …
-- src:1185 | (f) Section 251(e) of this title shall apply to a merger under this section.
-- src:1200 | Insofar as they may be applicable, the provisions set forth in the last sentence of § 252(c) of this title shall apply to a merger under this section, and the reference therein to “stockholder” shall be deemed to include “member” hereunder …
-- src:1226 | The requirements of § 252(d) of this title as to the appointment of the Secretary of State to receive process and the manner of serving the same in the event the surviving or resulting corporation is a foreign corporation shall also apply to mergers or consolidations effected under this section …
-- src:1218 | (d) Section 251(e) of this title shall apply to a merger under this section; § 251(d) of this title shall apply to any constituent stock corporation participating in a merger or consolidation under this section; and § 251(f) of this title shall apply to any constituent stock corporation participating in a merger under this section …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 255(c), (e), (f) (src:1182-1185); § 256(c) (src:1200); § 257(d) (src:1218); § 258(c) (src:1226)
DECLARE `dg7 Provision of s 251 or s 252 brought in by reference` IS ONE OF
    `the last sentence of s 251(c), a certificate of merger or consolidation in lieu of filing the agreement`
    `s 251(d), terminating or amending the agreement before it becomes effective`
    `s 251(e), the automatic amendment of the surviving corporation's certificate of incorporation`
    `s 251(f), no vote of the stockholders of a constituent corporation surviving a merger`
    `the last sentence of s 252(c), a certificate of merger or consolidation in lieu of filing the agreement`
    `s 252(d), the appointment of the Secretary of State to receive process`

-- The facts about the merger that decide whether a provision is brought in.
-- src:1202 | (e) Section § 251(e) of this title shall apply to a merger under this section if the corporation surviving the merger is a corporation of this State …
-- src:1218 | (d) Section 251(e) of this title shall apply to a merger under this section; § 251(d) of this title shall apply to any constituent stock corporation participating in a merger or consolidation under this section; and § 251(f) of this title shall apply to any constituent stock corporation participating in a merger under this section …
-- src:1226 | Section 251(e) of this title shall apply to mergers effected under this section if the surviving corporation is a corporation of this State; § 251(d) of this title shall apply to any constituent corporation participating in a merger or consolidation under this section (provided, however, that for purposes of a constituent nonstock corporation, references to the board of directors, to stockholders, and to shares shall be deemed to be references to the governing body of the corporation, to members of the corporation, and to memberships or membership interests of the corporation, as applicable, respectively); and § 251(f) of this title shall apply to any constituent stock corporation of this State participating in a merger under this section …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 256(e) (src:1202); § 257(d) (src:1218); § 258(c) (src:1226)
DECLARE `dg7 Context of a provision brought in` HAS
    `it is a merger and not a consolidation`                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the corporation surviving the merger is a corporation of this State`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the surviving or resulting corporation is a foreign corporation`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the constituent corporation concerned is a stock corporation of this State`     IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 255(c), (e), (f): the last sentence of s 251(c), s 251(d) and s 251(e) apply to a merger under this section; s 251(f) and the s 252
-- provisions are not brought in by s 255.
-- src:1182 | The provisions set forth in the last sentence of § 251(c) of this title shall apply to a merger under this section, and the reference therein to “stockholder” shall be deemed to include “member” hereunder …
-- src:1184 | (e) Section 251(d) of this title shall apply to a merger under this section; provided, however, that references to the board of directors, to stockholders, and to shares of a constituent corporation shall be deemed to be references to the governing body of the corporation …
-- src:1185 | (f) Section 251(e) of this title shall apply to a merger under this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 255(c) (src:1182); § 255(e) (src:1184); § 255(f) (src:1185)
GIVEN p IS A `dg7 Provision of s 251 or s 252 brought in by reference`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 255 the provision applies to a merger under this section` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `the last sentence of s 251(c), a certificate of merger or consolidation in lieu of filing the agreement`        THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 251(d), terminating or amending the agreement before it becomes effective`                                   THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 251(e), the automatic amendment of the surviving corporation's certificate of incorporation`                  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 251(f), no vote of the stockholders of a constituent corporation surviving a merger`                         THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the last sentence of s 252(c), a certificate of merger or consolidation in lieu of filing the agreement`       THEN FALSE
    WHEN `s 252(d), the appointment of the Secretary of State to receive process`                                       THEN FALSE

-- The reading s 255(e) gives to s 251(d) for a nonstock corporation: "references to the board of directors, to stockholders, and to
-- shares of a constituent corporation shall be deemed to be references to the governing body of the corporation, to members of the
-- corporation, and to memberships or membership interests, as applicable, respectively". The same words are in ss 256(f), 257(e) and 258(c).
-- src:1184 | provided, however, that references to the board of directors, to stockholders, and to shares of a constituent corporation shall be deemed to be references to the governing body of the corporation, to members of the corporation, and to memberships or membership interests, as applicable, respectively …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 255(e) (src:1184); § 256(f) (src:1203); § 257(e) (src:1219); § 258(c) (src:1226)
DECLARE `dg7 Reference in s 251(d)` IS ONE OF
    `a reference to the board of directors`
    `a reference to stockholders`
    `a reference to shares`

-- src:1184 | provided, however, that references to the board of directors, to stockholders, and to shares of a constituent corporation shall be deemed to be references to the governing body of the corporation, to members of the corporation, and to memberships or membership interests, as applicable, respectively …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 255(e) (src:1184); § 256(f) (src:1203); § 257(e) (src:1219); § 258(c) (src:1226)
DECLARE `dg7 Reference as read for a constituent nonstock corporation` IS ONE OF
    `a reference to the governing body of the corporation`
    `a reference to members of the corporation`
    `a reference to memberships or membership interests`

-- src:1184 | provided, however, that references to the board of directors, to stockholders, and to shares of a constituent corporation shall be deemed to be references to the governing body of the corporation, to members of the corporation, and to memberships or membership interests, as applicable, respectively …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 255(e) (src:1184); § 256(f) (src:1203); § 257(e) (src:1219); § 258(c) (src:1226)
GIVEN r IS A `dg7 Reference in s 251(d)`
GIVETH A `dg7 Reference as read for a constituent nonstock corporation`
`s 255(e) the reference in s 251(d) is read for a constituent nonstock corporation as` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `a reference to the board of directors` THEN `a reference to the governing body of the corporation`
    WHEN `a reference to stockholders`           THEN `a reference to members of the corporation`
    WHEN `a reference to shares`                 THEN `a reference to memberships or membership interests`

-- (g) The charitable limit. "Nothing in this section shall be deemed to authorize the merger of a charitable nonstock corporation into a
-- nonstock corporation if such charitable nonstock corporation would thereby have its charitable status lost or impaired; but a nonstock
-- corporation may be merged into a charitable nonstock corporation which shall continue as the surviving corporation." Whether charitable
-- status would be lost or impaired is a judgment (an input). READING F-255-2: the limit speaks of a MERGER "into" a nonstock corporation; a
-- consolidation into a new resulting corporation is not mentioned, so the limit does not bar it.
-- src:1186 | (g) Nothing in this section shall be deemed to authorize the merger of a charitable nonstock corporation into a nonstock corporation if such charitable nonstock corporation would thereby have its charitable status lost or impaired …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 255(g) (src:1186)
GIVEN kind IS A `dg7 Merger or consolidation`
      `the merging corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation`
      `the corporation it is merged into` IS A `Kind of corporation`
      `its charitable status would thereby be lost or impaired` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 255(g) this section does not authorize the merger` kind `the merging corporation` `the corporation it is merged into` `its charitable status would thereby be lost or impaired` MEANS
        kind EQUALS `a merger into a surviving corporation that is one of the constituent corporations`
    AND `the kind is a charitable nonstock corporation` `the merging corporation`
    AND `the kind is a nonstock corporation` `the corporation it is merged into`
    AND `its charitable status would thereby be lost or impaired`

-- src:1186 | but a nonstock corporation may be merged into a charitable nonstock corporation which shall continue as the surviving corporation …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 255(g) (src:1186)
GIVEN `the merging corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation`
      `the surviving corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 255(g) a nonstock corporation may be merged into a charitable nonstock corporation that continues as the surviving corporation` `the merging corporation` `the surviving corporation` MEANS
        `the kind is a nonstock corporation` `the merging corporation`
    AND `the kind is a charitable nonstock corporation` `the surviving corporation`

§ `s 256 Merger or consolidation of domestic and foreign nonstock corporations; service of process`

-- (a) "Any 1 or more nonstock corporations of this State may merge or consolidate with 1 or more foreign nonstock corporations, unless
-- the laws of the jurisdiction or jurisdictions under which such foreign nonstock corporation or corporations are organized prohibit
-- such merger or consolidation. The constituent corporations may merge into a single surviving corporation ... or they may consolidate
-- into a new resulting nonstock corporation formed by the consolidation, which may be a corporation of the jurisdiction of organization
-- of any 1 of the constituent corporations".
-- src:1190 | Any 1 or more nonstock corporations of this State may merge or consolidate with 1 or more foreign nonstock corporations, unless the laws of the jurisdiction or jurisdictions under which such foreign nonstock corporation or corporations are organized prohibit such merger or consolidation …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 256(a) (src:1190)
GIVEN constituents IS A LIST OF `dg7 Constituent corporation`
      kind IS A `dg7 Merger or consolidation`
      `the surviving corporation is one of the constituent corporations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resulting corporation is a new nonstock corporation of the jurisdiction of organization of one of the constituent corporations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the laws of a jurisdiction under which a foreign nonstock corporation is organized prohibit the merger or consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the law of another jurisdiction
      `the agreement complies, and is approved, in accordance with this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 256(a) the corporations may merge or consolidate` constituents kind `the surviving corporation is one of the constituent corporations` `the resulting corporation is a new nonstock corporation of the jurisdiction of organization of one of the constituent corporations` `the laws of a jurisdiction under which a foreign nonstock corporation is organized prohibit the merger or consolidation` `the agreement complies, and is approved, in accordance with this section` MEANS
        any `s 255(a) the corporation is a nonstock corporation of this State` constituents
    AND any `s 256(a) a foreign nonstock corporation` constituents
    AND all (GIVEN c YIELD `s 255(a) the corporation is a nonstock corporation of this State` c OR `s 256(a) a foreign nonstock corporation` c) constituents
    AND (NOT `the laws of a jurisdiction under which a foreign nonstock corporation is organized prohibit the merger or consolidation`)
    AND (IF kind EQUALS `a merger into a surviving corporation that is one of the constituent corporations`
         THEN `the surviving corporation is one of the constituent corporations`
         ELSE `the resulting corporation is a new nonstock corporation of the jurisdiction of organization of one of the constituent corporations`)
    AND `the agreement complies, and is approved, in accordance with this section`

-- (b) "All the constituent corporations shall enter into an agreement of merger or consolidation. The agreement shall state: (1) to (7)".
-- Items (3) and (4) bite only if the surviving or resulting corporation is a corporation of this State; item (7) adds what the laws of each
-- foreign jurisdiction require.
-- src:1191 | (b) All the constituent corporations shall enter into an agreement of merger or consolidation. The agreement shall state:
-- src:1194 | (3) In the case of a merger in which the surviving corporation is a corporation of this State, such amendments or changes in the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation as are desired to be effected by the merger (which amendments or changes may amend and restate the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation in its entirety), or, if no such amendments or changes are desired, a statement that the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation shall be its certificate of incorporation …
-- src:1195 | (4) In the case of a consolidation in which the resulting corporation is a corporation of this State, that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation shall be as is set forth in an attachment to the agreement …
-- src:1198 | (7) Such other provisions or facts as shall be required to be set forth in an agreement of merger or consolidation (including any provision for amendment of the certificate of incorporation (or equivalent document) of a surviving foreign nonstock corporation) by the laws of each jurisdiction under which any of the foreign nonstock corporations are organized …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 256(b) (src:1191-1198)
GIVEN kind IS A `dg7 Merger or consolidation`
      ag IS A `dg7 Agreement of merger or consolidation`
      `all the constituent corporations entered into the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the surviving or resulting corporation is a corporation of this State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 256(b) the agreement states what the subsection requires` kind ag `all the constituent corporations entered into the agreement` `the surviving or resulting corporation is a corporation of this State` MEANS
        `all the constituent corporations entered into the agreement`
    AND ag's `states the terms and conditions of the merger or consolidation`
    AND ag's `states the mode of carrying the merger or consolidation into effect`
    AND (   (NOT `the surviving or resulting corporation is a corporation of this State`)
         OR (IF kind EQUALS `a merger into a surviving corporation that is one of the constituent corporations`
             THEN ag's `states the amendments or changes in the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation, or that it shall be its certificate of incorporation`
             ELSE ag's `states that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation shall be as set forth in an attachment to the agreement`))
    AND (   (NOT ag's `some shares, memberships or membership interests are to be converted or cancelled`)
         OR ag's `states the manner of converting or cancelling them`)
    AND (   (NOT ag's `some shares, memberships or membership interests are not to remain outstanding`)
         OR ag's `states the cash, property, rights or securities the holders are to receive in exchange for them`)
    AND (   (NOT ag's `provides for the payment of cash in lieu of fractional shares, rights or other securities, or some other arrangement`)
         OR ag's `that provision is consistent with s 155`)
    AND ag's `states the provisions or facts the laws of each foreign jurisdiction require in an agreement of merger or consolidation`

-- (c) "The agreement shall be adopted, approved, certified, executed and acknowledged by each of the constituent corporations in
-- accordance with the laws under which it is organized and, in the case of a Delaware corporation, in the same manner as is provided in
-- s 255 of this title." A Delaware constituent is approved by `s 255 the constituent corporation has approved the agreement`; a foreign
-- constituent by its own law (an input). The agreement "shall be filed and shall become effective for all purposes of the laws of this State
-- when and as provided in s 255": the date is `s 255(c) the date on which the merger or consolidation becomes effective`.
-- src:1200 | (c) The agreement shall be adopted, approved, certified, executed and acknowledged by each of the constituent corporations in accordance with the laws under which it is organized and, in the case of a Delaware corporation, in the same manner as is provided in § 255 of this title …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 256(c) (src:1200)
DECLARE `s 256(c) Approval by one constituent corporation` HAS
    `where the corporation is formed`                                                                           IS A `Where an entity is formed`
    `the agreement was adopted, approved, certified, executed and acknowledged in accordance with the laws under which it is organized` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a Delaware corporation and was approved in the same manner as s 255 provides`                        IS A BOOLEAN   -- the outcome of `s 255 the constituent corporation has approved the agreement`

-- src:1200 | (c) The agreement shall be adopted, approved, certified, executed and acknowledged by each of the constituent corporations in accordance with the laws under which it is organized and, in the case of a Delaware corporation, in the same manner as is provided in § 255 of this title …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 256(c) (src:1200)
GIVEN a IS A `s 256(c) Approval by one constituent corporation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 256(c) the constituent corporation has approved the agreement as the subsection requires` a MEANS
        a's `the agreement was adopted, approved, certified, executed and acknowledged in accordance with the laws under which it is organized`
    AND (   (NOT a's `where the corporation is formed` EQUALS `this State`)
         OR a's `it is a Delaware corporation and was approved in the same manner as s 255 provides`)

-- (c) "Insofar as they may be applicable, the provisions set forth in the last sentence of s 252(c) of this title shall apply to a merger
-- under this section, and the reference therein to stockholder shall be deemed to include member hereunder." (e) "Section 251(e) shall
-- apply to a merger under this section if the corporation surviving the merger is a corporation of this State." (f) "Section 251(d) shall
-- apply to a merger under this section; provided, however, that references to the board of directors, to stockholders, and to shares ...
-- shall be deemed to be references to the governing body of the corporation, to members ... and to memberships or membership interests".
-- src:1200 | Insofar as they may be applicable, the provisions set forth in the last sentence of § 252(c) of this title shall apply to a merger under this section, and the reference therein to “stockholder” shall be deemed to include “member” hereunder …
-- src:1202 | (e) Section § 251(e) of this title shall apply to a merger under this section if the corporation surviving the merger is a corporation of this State …
-- src:1203 | (f) Section 251(d) of this title shall apply to a merger under this section; provided, however, that references to the board of directors, to stockholders, and to shares of a constituent corporation shall be deemed to be references to the governing body of the corporation, to members of the corporation, and to memberships or membership interests, as applicable, respectively …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 256(c) (src:1200); § 256(e) (src:1202); § 256(f) (src:1203)
GIVEN p IS A `dg7 Provision of s 251 or s 252 brought in by reference`
      ctx IS A `dg7 Context of a provision brought in`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 256 the provision applies to a merger under this section` p ctx MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `the last sentence of s 251(c), a certificate of merger or consolidation in lieu of filing the agreement`        THEN FALSE
    WHEN `s 251(d), terminating or amending the agreement before it becomes effective`                                   THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 251(e), the automatic amendment of the surviving corporation's certificate of incorporation`                  THEN ctx's `the corporation surviving the merger is a corporation of this State`
    WHEN `s 251(f), no vote of the stockholders of a constituent corporation surviving a merger`                         THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the last sentence of s 252(c), a certificate of merger or consolidation in lieu of filing the agreement`       THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 252(d), the appointment of the Secretary of State to receive process`                                       THEN FALSE

-- (d) Service of process. "If the corporation surviving or resulting from the merger or consolidation is a foreign nonstock corporation, it
-- shall agree that it may be served with process in this State in any proceeding for enforcement of any obligation of any constituent
-- corporation of this State, as well as for enforcement of any obligation of the surviving or resulting corporation arising from the merger
-- or consolidation and shall irrevocably appoint the Secretary of State as its agent to accept service of process in any suit or other
-- proceedings and shall specify the address to which a copy of such process shall be mailed by the Secretary of State."
-- src:1201 | (d) If the corporation surviving or resulting from the merger or consolidation is a foreign nonstock corporation, it shall agree that it may be served with process in this State in any proceeding for enforcement of any obligation of any constituent corporation of this State, as well as for enforcement of any obligation of the surviving or resulting corporation arising from the merger or consolidation and shall irrevocably appoint the Secretary of State as its agent to accept service of process in any suit or other proceedings and shall specify the address to which a copy of such process shall be mailed by the Secretary of State …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 256(d) (src:1201)
GIVEN `the surviving or resulting corporation is a foreign nonstock corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has agreed that it may be served with process in this State as the subsection describes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has irrevocably appointed the Secretary of State as its agent to accept service of process` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has specified the address to which a copy of the process shall be mailed by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 256(d) the surviving or resulting foreign nonstock corporation has done what the subsection requires of it` `the surviving or resulting corporation is a foreign nonstock corporation` `it has agreed that it may be served with process in this State as the subsection describes` `it has irrevocably appointed the Secretary of State as its agent to accept service of process` `it has specified the address to which a copy of the process shall be mailed by the Secretary of State` MEANS
        (NOT `the surviving or resulting corporation is a foreign nonstock corporation`)
    OR (       `it has agreed that it may be served with process in this State as the subsection describes`
         AND `it has irrevocably appointed the Secretary of State as its agent to accept service of process`
         AND `it has specified the address to which a copy of the process shall be mailed by the Secretary of State`)

-- "Process may be served upon the Secretary of State under this subsection by means of electronic transmission but only as prescribed by
-- the Secretary of State." (The Secretary of State's power to issue rules and regulations is machinery: no rule.)
-- src:1201 | Process may be served upon the Secretary of State under this subsection by means of electronic transmission but only as prescribed by the Secretary of State …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 256(d) (src:1201)
GIVEN `process is served by electronic transmission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the electronic transmission is as prescribed by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 256(d) the service of process on the Secretary of State is good` `process is served by electronic transmission` `the electronic transmission is as prescribed by the Secretary of State` MEANS
        (NOT `process is served by electronic transmission`)
    OR `the electronic transmission is as prescribed by the Secretary of State`

-- "In the event of such service upon the Secretary of State ..., the Secretary of State shall forthwith notify such surviving or resulting
-- corporation thereof by letter, directed to such corporation at its address so specified, unless such surviving or resulting corporation
-- shall have designated in writing to the Secretary of State a different address for such purpose, in which case it shall be mailed to the
-- last address so designated."
-- src:1201 | directed to such corporation at its address so specified, unless such surviving or resulting corporation shall have designated in writing to the Secretary of State a different address for such purpose, in which case it shall be mailed to the last address so designated …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 256(d) (src:1201)
GIVEN `the address the corporation specified` IS A STRING
      `the last address the corporation designated in writing to the Secretary of State for the purpose` IS A MAYBE STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`s 256(d) the address to which the Secretary of State's letter must be directed` `the address the corporation specified` `the last address the corporation designated in writing to the Secretary of State for the purpose` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last address the corporation designated in writing to the Secretary of State for the purpose`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the address the corporation specified`
    WHEN JUST designated THEN designated

-- "Such letter shall be sent by a mail or courier service that includes a record of mailing or deposit with the courier and a record of
-- delivery evidenced by the signature of the recipient. Such letter shall enclose a copy of the process and any other papers served upon
-- the Secretary of State."
-- src:1201 | In the event of such service upon the Secretary of State in accordance with this subsection, the Secretary of State shall forthwith notify such surviving or resulting corporation thereof by letter, directed to such corporation at its address so specified, unless such surviving or resulting corporation shall have designated in writing to the Secretary of State a different address for such purpose, in which case it shall be mailed to the last address so designated. Such letter shall be sent by a mail or courier service that includes a record of mailing or deposit with the courier and a record of delivery evidenced by the signature of the recipient. Such letter shall enclose a copy of the process and any other papers served upon the Secretary of State …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 256(d) (src:1201)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State notified the corporation forthwith by letter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the letter was sent by a mail or courier service with a record of mailing or deposit with the courier` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the service kept a record of delivery evidenced by the signature of the recipient` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the letter enclosed a copy of the process and any other papers served` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the letter was directed to the address the subsection requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 256(d) the Secretary of State's letter to the corporation is as the subsection requires` `the Secretary of State notified the corporation forthwith by letter` `the letter was sent by a mail or courier service with a record of mailing or deposit with the courier` `the service kept a record of delivery evidenced by the signature of the recipient` `the letter enclosed a copy of the process and any other papers served` `the letter was directed to the address the subsection requires` MEANS
        `the Secretary of State notified the corporation forthwith by letter`
    AND `the letter was sent by a mail or courier service with a record of mailing or deposit with the courier`
    AND `the service kept a record of delivery evidenced by the signature of the recipient`
    AND `the letter enclosed a copy of the process and any other papers served`
    AND `the letter was directed to the address the subsection requires`

-- "It shall be the duty of the plaintiff in the event of such service to serve process and any other papers in duplicate, to notify the
-- Secretary of State that service is being made pursuant to this subsection, and to pay the Secretary of State a fee as prescribed under
-- s 391(a)(29) of this title for the use of the State, which sum shall be taxed as a part of the costs in the proceeding if the plaintiff
-- shall prevail therein." (The amount of the fee is s 391(a)(29), piece dg11: whether it was paid is the fact.)
-- src:1201 | It shall be the duty of the plaintiff in the event of such service to serve process and any other papers in duplicate, to notify the Secretary of State that service is being made pursuant to this subsection, and to pay the Secretary of State a fee as prescribed under § 391(a)(29) of this title for the use of the State, which sum shall be taxed as a part of the costs in the proceeding if the plaintiff shall prevail therein …
