      `the plaintiff prevails in the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 256(d) the fee is taxed as a part of the costs in the proceeding` `the plaintiff paid the Secretary of State the fee prescribed under s 391(a)(29)` `the plaintiff prevails in the proceeding` MEANS
        `the plaintiff paid the Secretary of State the fee prescribed under s 391(a)(29)`
    AND `the plaintiff prevails in the proceeding`

-- "The Secretary of State shall maintain an alphabetical record of any such service setting forth the name of the plaintiff and
