-- "The Secretary of State shall not be required to retain such information for a period longer than 5 years from receipt of the
-- service of process." Not required to retain it after the fifth anniversary of the receipt; the fifth anniversary itself is inside the
-- 5 years (fork F-d1 applies to years as it does to days).
-- src:1201 | The Secretary of State shall not be required to retain such information for a period longer than 5 years from receipt of the service of process …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 256(d) (src:1201)
GIVEN `the date the service of process was received` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 256(d) the Secretary of State is no longer required to retain the record of the service` `the date the service of process was received` `the date on which the question is asked` MEANS
    `the date on which the question is asked` GREATER THAN `the date` (`period in years` 5) `after` `the date the service of process was received`

